WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:14.937
Passepartout headed quickly to the port to reserve three cabins on the Carnatic.

2
00:00:14.938 --> 00:00:19.071
He was delighted that Aouda was going to continue the journey with them.

3
00:00:19.072 --> 00:00:24.481
When he found Fix walking up and down the docks, he was not surprised.

4
00:00:24.482 --> 00:00:31.903
Fix seemed very worried. The detective had good reason to be upset—the warrant for Mr. Fogg's arrest had not arrived yet.

5
00:00:31.904 --> 00:00:35.087
It would not reach Hong Kong for two more days!

6
00:00:35.088 --> 00:00:42.053
Hong Kong was the last English territory on Mr. Fogg's route, and if Fix did not arrest him here, Fogg would escape.

7
00:00:42.054 --> 00:00:46.534
"Well, Monsieur Fix," said Passepartout as he caught up to the detective.

8
00:00:46.535 --> 00:00:49.720
"Have you decided to go with us as far as America?"

9
00:00:49.721 --> 00:00:53.742
"Yes," returned Fix through clenched teeth.

10
00:00:53.743 --> 00:01:02.128
"Good!" exclaimed Passepartout, laughing. "I knew you could not separate yourself from us. Come and purchase your ticket."

11
00:01:02.129 --> 00:01:07.014
Fix and Passepartout entered the steamer office and reserved four cabins.

12
00:01:07.015 --> 00:01:11.814
As the clerk handed them the tickets, he said that the repairs were complete on the Carnatic.

13
00:01:11.815 --> 00:01:16.915
The steamer would be ready to leave that evening, not the next morning as had been announced.

14
00:01:16.916 --> 00:01:20.653
"That will suit my master all the better," said Passepartout.

15
00:01:20.654 --> 00:01:22.885
"I will go and let him know."

16
00:01:22.886 --> 00:01:29.045
Fix decided to make a bold move. It was time to tell Passepartout the truth about his master.

17
00:01:29.046 --> 00:01:32.931
He invited Passepartout to go to a tavern on the quay.

18
00:01:32.932 --> 00:01:37.817
"I really should inform my master of the steamer's change in schedule," said Passepartout.

19
00:01:37.818 --> 00:01:43.210
"We'll just have a quick drink," Fix promised. "I want to tell you something."

20
00:01:43.211 --> 00:01:48.669
"Well . . . maybe just a quick one," Passepartout said with a smile.

21
00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:53.390
On entering the tavern, they noticed a large cot at the end of the room.

22
00:01:53.391 --> 00:01:59.613
Several people were lying on cushions, some were smoking from long pipes, and others were in a deep sleep.

23
00:01:59.614 --> 00:02:04.485
Passepartout realized, with mild surprise, that they were in an opium house.

24
00:02:04.486 --> 00:02:07.547
They ordered a bottle of wine and filled their glasses.

25
00:02:07.548 --> 00:02:11.242
"We must have a serious talk," said Fix.

26
00:02:11.243 --> 00:02:15.668
"A serious talk!" said Passepartout, emptying his glass.

27
00:02:15.669 --> 00:02:18.534
"Let's do that tomorrow. I don't have time now."

28
00:02:18.535 --> 00:02:22.926
"What I have to say concerns your master," said Fix.

29
00:02:22.927 --> 00:02:26.947
Passepartout looked at Fix, whose face had an odd expression.

30
00:02:26.948 --> 00:02:33.644
Fix placed his hand on Passepartout's arm and, lowering his voice, said, "You have guessed who I am?"

31
00:02:33.645 --> 00:02:37.017
"Of course!" said Passepartout, smiling.

32
00:02:37.018 --> 00:02:40.842
"Then I am going to tell you everything," Fix began.

33
00:02:40.843 --> 00:02:44.113
"But I know everything already," said Passepartout.

34
00:02:44.114 --> 00:02:48.248
"Those gentlemen have put themselves to a useless expense."

35
00:02:48.249 --> 00:02:55.248
"Useless?" said Fix with surprise. "It's clear that you don't know how large the sum is."

36
00:02:55.249 --> 00:02:59.865
"Of course I do," said Passepartout. "Twenty-thousand pounds!"

37
00:02:59.866 --> 00:03:03.548
"Fifty-five thousand!" said Fix.

38
00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:05.972
"What!" cried Passepartout.

39
00:03:05.973 --> 00:03:14.509
"Fifty-five thousand pounds," said Fix. "Now, if you help me, I'll share my reward with you."

40
00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:18.147
"Help you?" cried Passepartout, his eyes wide open.

41
00:03:18.148 --> 00:03:24.841
"Yes, help me keep Mr. Fogg here for two or three days," said Fix.

42
00:03:24.842 --> 00:03:30.297
"It's a conspiracy then! And it is organized by the gentlemen of the Reform Club!"

43
00:03:30.298 --> 00:03:35.941
Passepartout was outraged. "Mr. Fix, my master is an honorable man.

44
00:03:35.942 --> 00:03:41.298
He is trying to win the wager fairly, and you are trying to postpone him. Shame on you!"

45
00:03:41.299 --> 00:03:44.352
The detective passed his hand across his forehead.

46
00:03:44.353 --> 00:03:47.621
He would have to break the news delicately.

47
00:03:47.622 --> 00:03:54.505
"Listen to me," said Fix. "I am a police detective, sent here by the London office.

48
00:03:54.506 --> 00:03:59.243
Mr. Fogg's wager is only a pretext for leaving the country.

49
00:03:59.244 --> 00:04:08.926
On September 28, a sum of fifty-five-thousand pounds was stolen from the Bank of England. Phileas Fogg is the bank robber."

50
00:04:08.927 --> 00:04:13.766
"Nonsense!" yelled Passepartout, slamming his fist on the table.

51
00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:18.100
"Would you like to be arrested as his partner?" asked Fix abruptly.

52
00:04:18.101 --> 00:04:20.557
"No!" said Passepartout.

53
00:04:20.558 --> 00:04:26.702
"I advise you to help me detain him, or you risk just such an arrest," said Fix.

54
00:04:26.703 --> 00:04:31.993
"I refuse!" said Passepartout. He held his head between his hands.

55
00:04:31.994 --> 00:04:38.525
He couldn't believe what he was hearing. He filled his glass again and drank.

56
00:04:38.526 --> 00:04:41.464
Fix put his arm around Passepartout's shoulder.

57
00:04:41.465 --> 00:04:48.349
"If that is how you feel," he said in a companionable way, "please forget that I have said anything."

58
00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:54.182
Some pipes full of opium lay on the table, and Fix slipped one into Passepartout's hand.

59
00:04:54.183 --> 00:05:02.508
Passepartout drew several puffs. The smoke clouded around his head, and he fell unconscious on the table.

60
00:05:02.509 --> 00:05:09.657
While Fix was delaying Passepartout at the opium house, Mr. Fogg was escorting Aouda around the shops of Hong Kong.

61
00:05:09.658 --> 00:05:15.922
A lady, as Mr. Fogg was well aware, could not be expected to travel with only a carpetbag.

62
00:05:15.923 --> 00:05:19.467
In the evening they returned to the hotel for an elegant dinner.

63
00:05:19.468 --> 00:05:22.700
At bedtime Passepartout still had not returned.

64
00:05:22.701 --> 00:05:27.454
If Phileas Fogg could have been astonished by anything, this might have done it.

65
00:05:27.455 --> 00:05:32.653
But, thinking that the Carnatic was not departing until the morning, he was not concerned.

66
00:05:32.654 --> 00:05:40.140
The next morning Mr. Fogg and Aouda prepared their bags and arrived at the quay to learn that the Carnatic had sailed the evening before.

67
00:05:40.141 --> 00:05:49.490
Upon hearing the news, Mr. Fogg's comment to Aouda was simply, "It is an accident, madam. Nothing more."

68
00:05:49.491 --> 00:05:52.927
Well, there I was, asleep in an opium den!

69
00:05:52.928 --> 00:05:56.187
That Detective Fix, I hope I never see him again!

70
00:05:56.188 --> 00:06:00.056
Perhaps you had never heard of an opium den before reading about our adventures.

71
00:06:00.057 --> 00:06:05.732
Now you know that these dens are like bars where the drug opium is served and smoked through pipes.

72
00:06:05.733 --> 00:06:10.227
Beds are provided for people to lie down since opium makes people sleepy.

73
00:06:10.228 --> 00:06:13.698
Opium is a highly addictive drug made from poppies.

74
00:06:13.699 --> 00:06:21.067
It was used as a medicine in China starting in the fifteenth century but was banned in the eighteenth century due to its harmful effects.

75
00:06:21.068 --> 00:06:26.479
Despite the ban opium use in China flourished, and many Chinese people became addicted.

76
00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:31.967
That was because a powerful British company called the East India Company started growing opium in India

77
00:06:31.968 --> 00:06:35.373
and smuggling it into China in huge amounts!

78
00:06:35.374 --> 00:06:39.394
This business was so profitable that the British government let it continue.

79
00:06:39.395 --> 00:06:45.013
The Chinese went to war with the British twice to stop the smuggling, but the British won both times.

80
00:06:45.014 --> 00:06:49.154
As Chinese people emigrated around the world, they brought opium with them.

81
00:06:49.155 --> 00:06:57.861
Soon opium dens spread to large cities such as London and San Francisco.
